
======================================================================================================================
CFG499  option A (lenient black holes) as a full track on the C-H/K chassis
======================================================================================================================
Action: sqrt(-g)[R - lambda K^2 + alpha a.a], 16 pi G = 1, beta = 0, lambda = c_2, alpha = alpha_c.
Scope of test (1): O(v), l = 1, Schwarzschild + the test-khronon background; first metric-khronon round trip
F0 -> h1 -> F1, local at the UH (generalised Frobenius in x = r - r_UH) plus the boundary-condition count.

======================================================================================================================
S0  the angle-integrated quadratic Lagrangian of the full action for the l = 1 sector (sympy)
======================================================================================================================
    loaded the cached derivation (l1PN.srepr in the system temp dir)
    background khronon kept as P = H'(r) and lapse N0 (identity N0^-2 = -2P - eP^2); bilinear terms: KK 92, AA 68, EH 58
    linear curvature of the l = 1 metric perturbation: Kretschmann_0 = 48/r**6, 12 Riemann components

======================================================================================================================
K1  flat-space khronon dispersion WITH metric mixing, from the same Lagrangian engine
======================================================================================================================
    tensor: -(k - omega)*(k + omega); scalar-sector determinant gcd: k**2*omega*(alpha*k**2*lambda + 3*alpha*lambda*omega**2 + 2*alpha*omega**2 - 2*k**2*lambda)
  [PASS] K1 flat space: omega^2 = c_S^2 k^2 with c_S^2 = lambda (2 - alpha)/(alpha (2 + 3 lambda)) exactly, tensor speed 1
         measured: omega^2 = [k**2*lambda*(2 - alpha)/(alpha*(3*lambda + 2))]

