======================================================================================================================
K3  Einstein-Hilbert block gauge invariance, and 1c(i) the homogeneous Einstein l = 1 solutions
======================================================================================================================
  [PASS] K3 a pure-gauge l = 1 h = L_xi g (xi = (xi0 cos, xi1 cos, -xi2 sin, 0)) annihilates all six Einstein-Hilbert Euler-Lagrange equations identically
         measured: residuals [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
    gauge C = E = Kf = 0 vacuum system: E_A -> B = C1; E_E -> D = C1*r - C1 + r**2*Derivative(A(r), r)/2; E_B -> A = -2*C1/r + C2/r**2 + C3*r
    remaining equations after substitution: [0, 0, -2*C3, 0, 0, 0]; constants [C1, C2, C3], constraint solution [{C3: 0}]
    residual gauge (C, E, Kf preserved: [0, 0, 0]) is 2-dimensional (c1, c2): A = 2*(-c1 - c2*r)/r**2, B = c2, D = 2*c1/r + c2*r
  [PASS] 1c(i) every homogeneous solution of the gauge-fixed Einstein l = 1 block is pure gauge: solution-space dimension = residual-gauge dimension = 2 (no physical l = 1 constant, none excluded anywhere, so no condition is added)
         measured: dimension 2 vs residual gauge 2

